      "title": "Text (Prompt)",
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "PrimitiveStringMultiline"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "[Segment 1]\nStyle: dream physics, deep-blue monochrome with a misty diffusion in the glow, shadows keeping faint layers instead of pure black, spatial scale distortion, photoreal texture.\nAction: [0s-1.5s] The projected face breathes with light shifts, dust drifting, his silhouette still; [1.5s-4s] The camera pulls back slowly and the giant face shrinks with it, revealing that this colossal face floats on the wall of a vast bedroom: a projection inside a dream-room, his silhouette standing at the bedside looking up; [4s-8s] The camera keeps pulling back past the room's boundary as the walls curl inward like paper, folding into the darkness of a second dream layer, the giant face shrinking with the curling walls into a floating glowing mask suspended in the void, the man motionless and looking up throughout, the frame ending with the mask hovering directly above him. No text. Camera: one continuous pull-back, slight warping as the space folds, no cuts. Audio: a low drone wrapped in an underwater-feeling muted reverb, paper-like stretching as the space curls, one distant bell.\n\n[Segment 2]\nStyle: same dreamy haze, the blue one shade darker, a deeper dream layer.\nAction: [0s-2s] The glowing mask rotates slowly above him; he raises a hand, and the instant his fingertips near it the whole space collapses in scale: the mask becomes a reflection inside a pupil, his body edge receding into silhouette; [2s-5s] The viewpoint reveals itself as his eye all along: the frame wavers slightly, we have been looking through his pupil, the blue iris texture rings into view at the frame's edge; [5s-8s] The giant face in the pupil breathes once with light, the dream begins to dissolve: the image tears slightly like a bad signal, the reflection flickers twice, locking finally on the extreme eye close-up, a deeper blue surfacing slowly in the depths of the iris. No text. Camera: an objective view snapping into pupil-POV, the switch made through a slight signal-tear, no cuts. Audio: a heartbeat approaching to become the main beat, one falling bass note as the mask shrinks, signal noise through the tear, every sound sucked away on the last beat leaving a faint ringing in the ears.\n\n[Shared]\nDreamy haze over the blue monochrome, faint layers in the shadows, photoreal texture, spatial scale distorting with each dream layer. Negative: no water ripples, no third-person frontal face, no color shift away from the blue monochrome, no text overlays, no subtitles, no dissolve transitions, no extra light sources, no logo."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 17,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
